    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0510" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg404"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Denby reports that riots may be expected throughout China, and that the
                    situation is serious; that riots were in progress at Nanking and other places;
                    that two foreigners had been murdered at Wusueh, and that the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Palos</hi> had gone there, but that so far no Americans
                    had been injured. He also states that the Emperor delays issuing edict for the
                    protection of foreigners.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
